  "accepted_interpretation": [
    "All eight sampled C_m-by-grid points converged and satisfy the frozen numerical/QA conditions.",
    "On both 20- and 40-cell grids, maximum static pressure and maximum static temperature decrease across the sampled C_m sequence 25 -> 30 -> 42.5 -> 60, consistent with the teacher closure producing longer mixing length and weaker in-domain mixing/combustion as C_m increases.",
    "Minimum Mach is not promoted as a monotonic function of C_m: the low-C_m ordering differs between the 20- and 40-cell grids, demonstrating coupled response and grid sensitivity.",
    "The 20-to-40 relative changes in the reported extrema decrease substantially toward the high-C_m end, but the two-grid study is only a robustness diagnostic and does not establish formal grid independence.",
    "The Eq.11.20 project-geometry crossover near C_m=31.684 helps separate samples that can versus cannot reach complete mixing before the project combustor exit; it is not an optimum, calibrated value, or combustion-mode boundary."
  ]
